CHANGELOG.md	- After a downgrade to an older server, a person whose walls use the new settings (tool rules, push rules, recording, auto-stop, or Azure DevOps or GitHub capabilities) gets errors when they create a run, until they run `wardyn walls delete` or save their walls without those settings.	the rc.12 release changelog names the real command, wardyn walls clear
CHANGELOG.md	- An organisation's remote MCP server can be sent the run's signed identity, so its gateway knows which person, run and runner made each call: set "Token audience" in the server's component editor (`mcp.gateway_audience`). Turn run identity on for a model provider first; a run whose servers and providers share one audience at different addresses is refused.	moved into the single Added list when the duplicate Added heading was merged
CHANGELOG.md	- Docs: a new page on signing people in to a custom model endpoint, and a new page on checking image signatures in your cluster with Sigstore policy-controller or Kyverno. The second recipe is not run in CI.	moved into the single Added list when the duplicate Added heading was merged
CHANGELOG.md	- The run page's VM desktop tile is clearer. It says how to type and click on macOS 26 (`wardyn window <run-id>`), says when the gateway check failed (with Try again) instead of showing nothing, shows a pause or resume error under its buttons, and no longer shows a View only chip beside Off. Files on a VM says copy and paste aren't available, a macOS disk that couldn't be removed says who to tell, a Watch desktop error wraps instead of being cut off, and the Identity card has a Machine row and separate Started and Started by rows.	the tile now offers an Open Mac window button instead of printing the command
CHANGELOG.md	- A `github_capabilities` list without `code_write`, in your walls or the run's policy, now stops git pushes to GitHub: the git broker refuses them with a sentence saying why (`brokered:git:push-capability`), and the run's GitHub tokens are read-only. An `azure_devops_capabilities` list without `code_write` does the same for an Azure DevOps `git_pat` lane.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- An `image` capability grant may be a registry or path prefix ending in `/*` (for example `registry.example.com/team/*`), so one grant covers every image under it. A deny on an image also covers its other spellings, such as capitals in the host, `:443` and Docker Hub short names.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- An admin can set a model provider's run identity token to live 60 to 600 seconds (`gateway_identity.token_lifetime_seconds`; the default stays 10 minutes), so a killed run's tokens stop working sooner	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- Docs: Windows VMs are listed as not available yet. A Linux desktop VM uses your own image for now.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- Docs: joining a run to a platform team's own kernel sensor on Kubernetes.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- Docs: the macOS VM page now covers the attended window (how to open it, the site switch, every refusal, closing, audit rows) and an interactive developer sandbox quickstart.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- Kept machines in the console: New run and Review offer keeping the machine or resuming a kept one, the run page's Machine card shows the machine as it is now and flags one that still needs cleanup, Your settings lists your kept machines with their idle days, and an admin sets the site switch and a governance profile's `deny_kept_machines`. A kept machine's expiry is now the one its Mac wrote at the stop, so the Mac and Wardyn agree on one deadline; a stop that could not write it reports the expiry as pending. The macOS VM page and the SDK reference cover keeping a machine, what stays on its disk, its expiry, deletion, limits and the API.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- Opening an app from Attach from your terminal now opens its new tab inside your click, and says to allow pop-ups when the browser blocks it. The SSH lane opens by default when you have a key, and the VS Code Remote-SSH reason no longer says the sandbox has no internet.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- Your walls can now also narrow tool rules, push rules, recording, auto-stop and Azure DevOps and GitHub capabilities, and the Settings card keeps them across a save.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- `push_rules.deny_all`, in a policy or your walls, refuses every push: git pushes on every broker lane, ref updates and deletes included, and Azure DevOps REST writes to a repository. The built-in Read-only and Sealed wall presets now set it, so they refuse pushes. A run that sets it is refused at start when it holds an `ssh_key`, or a `git_pat` while the git token broker is off (`push_deny_all_ssh_key`, `push_deny_all_resident_pat`).	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
CHANGELOG.md	- `wardyn window <run>` opens a window onto your macOS VM run on your own Mac, `wardyn window <run> --status` shows whether one can open and why your last one closed, and `wardyn run --machine-kind macos_vm --window` asks for it as the VM comes up. A refusal prints the server's sentence and exits non-zero. Built and unit-tested; not yet run on a real Mac.	rc.12 changelog at the cut: reworded, folded into a fuller bullet, or moved under the single Added heading
